Yep — a few things are off:

1. You’re mixing raw <link> tags inside the <SEO /> component props. The SEO component only takes props; you shouldn’t place elements between its opening and closing tags.


2. <ClientRouter /> is in the <head>. It belongs in the body and should wrap your content.


3. Your Open Graph type is set to "image/jpeg" (that’s a MIME type). It should be something like "website" or "article".


4. You’re defining favicon links twice (once manually and again via extend.link). Pick one.


5. Using is:inline together with a src attribute is unnecessary; keep src and drop is:inline (or inline the code and keep is:inline).



Here’s a cleaned, working layout:

---
// BaseLayout.astro
import { ClientRouter } from "astro:transitions";
import "../styles/global.css";
import { SEO } from "astro-seo";

import SmoothScroll from "../components/SmoothScroll.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

import "@fontsource/open-sans/400.css";
import openSansWoff2 from "@fontsource/open-sans/files/open-sans-latin-400-normal.woff2";

type Props = { title: string; description?: string };
const { title, description = "Jannis Reinelt" } = Astro.props;

// Current page value (/home, /about, /404 ...)
const currentPage =
  Astro.url.pathname.replace(/\/$/, "").split("/").pop() || "home";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-page={currentPage}>
  <head>
    <SEO
      title={title}
      description={description}
      charset="UTF-8"
      openGraph={{
        basic: {
          title,
          type: "website", // not a MIME type
          image: "/jannisreinelt-og.jpg",
        },
      }}
      extend={{
        link: [
          // Choose ONE set of favicon links; these cover common cases:
          { rel: "icon", type: "image/svg+xml", href: "/favicon/favicon.svg" },
          { rel: "icon", type: "image/png", sizes: "32x32", href: "/favicon/favicon-32x32.png" },
          { rel: "icon", type: "image/png", sizes: "16x16", href: "/favicon/favicon-16x16.png" },
          { rel: "apple-touch-icon", sizes: "180x180", href: "/favicon/apple-touch-icon.png" },
          { rel: "manifest", href: "/favicon/site.webmanifest" },
          { rel: "sitemap", href: "/sitemap-index.xml" },

          // Preload your font (note: keep "crossorigin" lowercased)
          {
            rel: "preload",
            href: openSansWoff2,
            as: "font",
            type: "font/woff2",
            crossorigin: "anonymous",
          },
        ],
        meta: [
          { name: "twitter:image", content: "/jannisreinelt-og.jpg" },
          { name: "twitter:title", content: title },
          { name: "twitter:description", content: description },
          { name: "viewport", content: "width=device-width,initial-scale=1" },
          { name: "msapplication-TileColor", content: "#000000" },
          { name: "theme-color", content: "#ffffff" },
          { name: "generator", content: Astro.generator },
          // Optional: app title for iOS PWA icon
          { name: "apple-mobile-web-app-title", content: "MyWebSite" },
        ],
      }}
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <ClientRouter>
      <SmoothScroll />
      <Header />
      <slot />
      <Footer />
    </ClientRouter>

    <!-- Keep scripts external OR inline; don't combine src + is:inline -->
    <script src={`/scripts/initVideo.js?v=${Date.now()}`} type="module"></script>
    <script id="hlsjs" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/hls.js@1.5.11/dist/hls.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="/scripts/themeToggle.js" type="module"></script>
    <script src="/scripts/langToggle.js" type="module"></script>
    <script src="/scripts/videoAutoPlay.js" type="module"></script>
    <script src="/scripts/mailcopy.js" type="module"></script>
  </body>
</html>

Why this fixes it:

<SEO ... /> is now self-closing with only props; no stray <link> tags inside.

Client routing wraps your visible UI in the body, not the head.

OG config uses a valid type.

Favicon/meta are defined exactly once via extend.

Scripts are consistent (either external with src or inline with is:inline).


If you want Apple’s “Add to Home Screen” niceties (standalone display, status bar style, etc.), we can extend with a few PWA meta tags + a minimal manifest.json.

